    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the build/test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, identified by the calendar year it *ends* in \u2014 the standard AU convention), all derived from the already-business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` the controller writes back onto the owner.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `mapper/FiscalYearResolver.java`: a static utility mirroring the other resolvers, with:\n- `fiscalYear(date)` \u2014 4-digit fiscal year (month \u2265 July \u2192 `year+1`, else `year`)\n- `deriveFiscalYear(date)` \u2014 the `FY<YY>` label (null-safe)\n- `elapsedFiscalYears(from, to)` \u2014 whole fiscal years crossed\n\n**Changes to existing behaviour:**\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` mapping (`FY<YY>`), and changed `membershipNumber`'s year segment from the raw registration-year to the fiscal-year `%02d`.\n- `MembershipLevelResolver` \u2014 tenure now counts *elapsed fiscal years* (`> 1`) instead of a 365-day window; dropped the `ChronoUnit` days math.\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1` \u2014 the audit-log membership number now uses the fiscal year too, keeping it consistent with the mapped DTO.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` property to `OwnerDto` (which regenerates the `OwnerDto` class at build time) and updated the `membershipNumber`/`membershipPoints` descriptions.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreReturnsFiscalYear`) passes; the audit line confirms `registrationDate=2026-09-11 \u2026 membershipNumber=NSW-\u2026-M27` \u2014 September falls after 1 July, so it correctly resolves to **FY27**. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
